## Examples

### Good Developer Defect Entry:

```markdown
| DEF-001 | 🟠 High | FormManager.ChangeStatusAsync missing | FormManager | Tests call `ChangeStatusAsync` but method doesn't exist. Current `SetStatus()` uses sync database calls.<br/><br/>**Root Cause:** Method never implemented as async.<br/><br/>**Proper Fix:**<br/>• Rename to `ChangeStatusAsync`<br/>• Use `await SaveChangesAsync()`<br/>• Use `await FirstOrDefaultAsync()`<br/><br/>**Wrong Fix:** ❌ Wrapping sync `SetStatus()` in `Task.Run()`<br/><br/>**Workaround:** None | 1. Run test: ESOURCE2-2147_FormStatus/PositiveTests.cs<br/>2. Call `_fixture.FormManager.ChangeStatusAsync(formId, status)` | Method executes and changes form status using proper async/await | Compilation error: method not found. Current sync implementation blocks threads. | Dev | `CS1061: 'FormManager' does not contain a definition for 'ChangeStatusAsync'` | FormStatusTests.cs:45 | 2026-01-26 | Open | QA Team |
```

### Good QA Issue Entry:

```markdown
| QA-001 | 🟡 Medium | Incomplete async wrappers in ManagerExtensions | Infrastructure | Many manager methods lack async wrappers. This is a **temporary workaround** only while developers implement proper async managers.<br/><br/>**Root Cause:** Managers implemented synchronously, tests expect async.<br/><br/>**Temporary Fix (QA):** Add more extension wrappers<br/><br/>**Permanent Fix:** DEF-009 - Make underlying managers truly async | 1. Review ManagerExtensions.cs<br/>2. Compare against test expectations<br/>3. Identify missing async wrappers | All test-required methods have temporary async wrappers | Only partial coverage (~30%) with sync-wrapped-as-async methods | Local/CI | 45 tests blocked | DEF-009 | 2026-01-26 | Open | QA Team |
```

