## Compliance Checklist

When adding or updating defects, ensure:

### Required for ALL defects:
- [ ] Correct file chosen (Developer vs QA)
- [ ] Correct ID prefix used (DEF-XXX vs QA-XXX)
- [ ] **Severity assigned** (🔴/🟠/🟡/🟢)
- [ ] **Component/Category specified**
- [ ] Clear, descriptive title (max 60 chars)
- [ ] Detailed description with root cause (if known)
- [ ] Clear reproduction steps (numbered)
- [ ] Expected vs actual results
- [ ] **Environment specified** (Dev/Staging/Prod/CI)
- [ ] Date in ISO format (YYYY-MM-DD)
- [ ] Status correctly set
- [ ] Reporter identified

### Recommended:
- [ ] Error message/log snippet included
- [ ] Related test case referenced
- [ ] Screenshots/evidence attached (for UI issues)
- [ ] Workaround documented (if available)
- [ ] Cross-references added (if applicable)
- [ ] Impact quantified (tests blocked, users affected)

### For Resolution:
- [ ] Resolution notes explain the fix
- [ ] Fixed by developer identified
- [ ] Fix commit/PR referenced
- [ ] Fix version specified
- [ ] Verified by QA
- [ ] Verification date recorded
- [ ] Moved to Resolved section
